.SH SOLVING ISSUES
.PP
.PD 0
.IP 1. 4
At startup Waybar fails with \fB"error while loading shared libraries: libcava.\&so: cannot open shared object file: No such file or directory"\fR.\&
This happens when libcava has not been registered in the system library cache.\& Run \fBsudo ldconfig\fR to refresh the cache.\&
This can also occur when Waybar is installed under \fB/usr/local\fR but libcava is elsewhere.\& To fix it:
 1.\& Remove the local libcava installation: \fBsudo rm \-rfv /usr/local/include/cava /usr/local/lib64/pkgconfig/cava.\&pc /usr/local/lib64/libcava.\&so\fR
 2.\& Reconfigure Waybar to use the system prefix: \fBmeson configure build \-Dprefix="/usr"\fR
 3.\& Rebuild Waybar: \fBninja \-C build\fR
 4.\& Install Waybar: \fBsudo meson install \-C build\fR
.PD
.PP
.PD 0
.IP 1. 4
Waybar starts but the cava module does not react to audio.\&
 1.\& First, verify that standalone cava works correctly.\&
 2.\& If it does, comment out all Waybar cava options, uncomment \fBcava_config\fR, and point it to the working cava configuration file.\&
 3.\& The \fBinput_delay\fR may be too large or too small.\& Try setting it to 4 seconds, restart Waybar, and check again after that delay.\& This is usually sufficient, even on slower machines.\&
 4.\& You may have accidentally toggled pause mode via an action.\&
.PD
.PP
.SH REPORTING ISSUES
.PP
This module is a consumer of the cava API.\& For bugs in the cava engine itself, please report them to [cava upstream](https://github.\&com/karlstav/cava) first.\&
.PP
Upstream cava does not provide a shared library.\& The Waybar cava module uses [libcava](https://github.\&com/LukashonakV/cava), a fork maintained by the module author, to provide one.\& If the issue is specific to the shared library packaging, report it to libcava.\&
.PP
When requesting a new upstream cava release to be packaged in libcava, open an issue at libcava with the title `[Bump] x.\&x.\&x`, where `x.\&x.\&x` is the desired cava version.\&
.PP
